{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06J1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fb6ad280346362a580dd3b1ba5464da5eea3146f40ecf0a8f3a682476d6fa006", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cf6551114dc4c9138dae71d2df46ab08b6d77093145385e0961184dea89ca893", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThere is a very natural property of categories cofibred in groupoids\nover <MATH_0001> which is easy to check in practice\nand which implies Schlessinger's properties (S1) and (S2) we\nhave introduced earlier.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:faee96af8591d543e82964486ea51f174cd7c4ecc4d33a4d3cf34d0c87e7461f", "unit_id": "tag:06J1:prose-0001"}
